	(text "REAL-TIME CLOCK (hardware design section 14).\nU10 PCF8563T at I2C address 0x51 on I2C0. It keeps time down to 1.0 V.\nD10 and D11 are silicon diodes, not Schottky: a Schottky leaks as much as the RTC draws.\nVDD_RTC is about 2.7 V from 3V3 and 2.6 V from the cell. R59 limits the current into the\ncell to under 1 mA if D11 fails short.\nY1 32.768 kHz, 12.5 pF. C36 18 pF with the 25 pF inside OSCO gives an 11.7 pF load.\nCLKO is not used: firmware writes 0x00 to register 0x0D to turn the 32 kHz output off.\nBT1 holds a CR2032, fitted at final assembly. Back-up current 0.25 uA typical: about ten years."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 139.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9164d90b-15f4-54f2-923a-02a0b9d8224b")
	)
	(text "Real-time clock with coin-cell backup"
